30:21.260 --> 30:23.180
J is an anti-symmetric real matrix.

30:23.740 --> 30:25.780
Geometrically, it's very simple to visualize.

30:26.440 --> 30:31.120
It represents a perfect quarter turn, a 90 degree rotation in a 2D plane.

30:31.320 --> 30:31.620
Okay.

30:31.920 --> 30:36.040
Crucially, it is the real number matrix that behaves exactly like the imaginary number I.

30:36.260 --> 30:40.580
Right, because if you take a vector pointing north and you rotate it 90 degrees,

30:40.580 --> 30:42.100
that's 1 J, it points west.

30:42.220 --> 30:42.300
Yeah.

30:42.380 --> 30:45.840
If you rotate it 90 degrees again, a second J, it points south.

30:46.100 --> 30:46.340
Right.

30:46.520 --> 30:50.320
It's pointing in the exact negative opposite direction of where it started.

30:50.460 --> 30:53.760
So J squared equals negative 1, just like I squared equals negative 1.

30:53.880 --> 30:54.320
Exactly.

30:54.540 --> 30:55.680
But why is it invisible?

30:55.960 --> 30:58.220
Why couldn't we see it in our parameter counting?

30:58.400 --> 30:58.620
Yeah.

30:58.820 --> 30:59.600
Why couldn't we see it?

30:59.600 --> 31:01.240
Because J is anti-symmetric.

31:02.080 --> 31:08.400
In real number quant mechanics, local observables, the actual physical dials you can turn in

31:08.400 --> 31:11.120
your lab, must be symmetric matrices.

31:11.480 --> 31:11.720
Okay.

31:12.040 --> 31:15.820
Anti-symmetric matrices do not correspond to valid local measurements.

31:16.040 --> 31:19.440
You can never observe J in your lab, and I can never observe J in mine.

31:19.440 --> 31:24.060
But when you use the tensor product to combine them, when you do J tensor J.

31:24.880 --> 31:29.840
The rules of matrix algebra dictate that the tensor product of two anti-symmetric matrices

31:29.840 --> 31:32.160
results in a symmetric matrix.

31:32.300 --> 31:34.540
J tensor J is perfectly symmetric.

31:35.260 --> 31:40.620
Therefore, it is a completely valid physical observable measurement on the joint system.

31:41.060 --> 31:46.880
But because its constituent parts are locally impossible to observe, you can never construct

31:46.880 --> 31:47.980
it from your local notes.

31:48.140 --> 31:49.440
I'm trying to picture this physically.

31:49.600 --> 31:55.000
It's like, imagine a massive bank vault that requires two physical keys to be turned at

31:55.000 --> 31:56.480
the exact same millisecond.

31:56.540 --> 31:56.720
Okay.

31:56.800 --> 31:57.400
I like this.

31:57.820 --> 32:03.740
But the weird part is, neither you nor I can even see our own keyholes when we are standing

32:03.740 --> 32:04.760
in our separate labs.

32:05.180 --> 32:07.220
The keyholes literally don't exist locally.

32:07.260 --> 32:07.580
Right.

32:07.580 --> 32:11.940
They only pop into physical existence when we bring the two vaults together into a single

32:11.940 --> 32:14.220
room and look at them as a unified whole.

32:14.460 --> 32:16.060
That is a fantastic visualization.

32:16.060 --> 32:17.960
The keyholes only exist globally.

32:18.140 --> 32:20.860
And this isn't just an abstract mathematical quirk either.

32:21.400 --> 32:26.160
The text proves that this invisible parameter, which we can call C, represents a whole family

32:26.160 --> 32:27.100
of physical states.

32:27.560 --> 32:31.760
The parameter C can slide on a scale anywhere between Megas 1 and 1.

32:31.960 --> 32:32.540
Meaning what?

32:32.760 --> 32:39.100
Meaning there is an entire continuous spectrum of physical realities, an entire interval of

32:39.100 --> 32:46.320
valid joint states that are completely 100% indistinguishable from each other to any local observer.

32:46.640 --> 32:46.760
Wow.

32:47.460 --> 32:50.160
Which brings us perfectly to the concept of entanglement.

32:50.520 --> 32:55.660
Because this invisible parameter C fundamentally redefines what we mean by that word.

32:55.780 --> 32:56.560
It absolutely does.

32:56.560 --> 33:02.300
And to understand the illusion of entanglement here, we have to explore a mathematical tool

33:02.300 --> 33:03.660
called the partial trace.

33:03.860 --> 33:04.520
The partial trace.

33:05.000 --> 33:06.260
It sounds like an auditing term.

33:06.520 --> 33:07.620
How does it work physically?

33:07.960 --> 33:11.260
Think of it as the mathematical operation of ignoring a subsystem.

33:11.480 --> 33:12.980
It's how we calculate shadows.

33:13.180 --> 33:13.900
Calculating shadows.

33:13.900 --> 33:19.060
Suppose you and I share a joint quantum state, but you take your half to Mars, and I keep

33:19.060 --> 33:19.940
my half on Earth.

33:20.340 --> 33:20.680
Okay.

33:20.840 --> 33:24.680
If I want to calculate what I will see in my lab on Earth, I can't measure your system.

33:24.940 --> 33:29.460
I have to mathematically trace out or average over all the possibilities of your half of

33:29.460 --> 33:29.880
the system.

33:29.980 --> 33:31.020
I marginalize it.

33:31.060 --> 33:34.140
Imagine two synchronized dancers in a pitch black room.

33:34.820 --> 33:40.320
If I only have one spotlight and I shine it entirely on dancer A, I am essentially applying

33:40.320 --> 33:42.120
a partial trace to dancer B.

33:42.120 --> 33:48.200
I'm ignoring dancer B's specific movements and just looking at the chaotic, seeming shadow

33:48.200 --> 33:51.440
dancer A is casting based on their unseen interaction.

33:51.560 --> 33:52.100
Exactly.

33:52.260 --> 33:53.120
That is a great analogy.

33:53.680 --> 33:59.140
When you apply this partial trace operation to our invisible J tensor J direction, the math

33:59.140 --> 34:00.900
is totally unambiguous.

34:01.100 --> 34:03.560
The partial trace completely annihilates it.

34:03.780 --> 34:04.220
Annihilates it.

34:04.240 --> 34:07.640
If you trace out my system, the J tensor J term drops to zero.

34:08.200 --> 34:10.260
If I trace out your system, it drops to zero.

34:10.260 --> 34:15.420
From either local perspective, this joint state looks entirely devoid of structure.

34:15.580 --> 34:16.620
It looks like pure static.

34:16.740 --> 34:18.180
It looks maximally mixed.

34:18.340 --> 34:18.500
Okay.

34:18.600 --> 34:24.580
So the state has this deeply hidden structure globally, the two keyholes, but locally it

34:24.580 --> 34:26.000
just looks like random static.

34:26.140 --> 34:26.360
Yeah.

34:26.440 --> 34:28.660
That sounds exactly like the definition of entanglement.

34:28.780 --> 34:31.680
And this is where the author delivers an absolute knockout punch.

34:31.900 --> 34:33.500
This is the crux of the entire text.

